--- IR --->
// the empty value of each shape, at an argument the parser could not type. a wrapped `T?` is a
// cleared tag, then argument_abi_for's integer of the alloc size rather than a first-class
// `{ i1, T }`. the free shape is a null handle. before the binding the null had no type at
// all and every one of these was a `ptr null`, which for the two wrapped parameters is not
// even the right *width*, let alone the right value
//
// the integer is loaded from the natural slot (fieldwise store, then `load i64` / `load i96`).
// a pad-plus-memcpy of those bytes is the shape that blocked SROA on every inlined caller
//
// `MQ` is the nullable level and what follows it is the payload's own mangling, so a wrapped one reads
// `MQMLPi` where a class handle - whose `?` is a flag on one address rather than a pair - reads `MQLC4Node`
CHECK: define i32 @main(
CHECK: load i64, ptr %arg.slot
CHECK: call i32 @_tag_ofZZMQMLPi(i64
CHECK: load i96, ptr %arg.slot1
CHECK: call i32 @_x_ofZZMQMLC5Point(i96
CHECK: call i32 @_node_tagZZMQLC4Node(ptr null)
// a member call's written null is argument 1, behind the receiver, and takes the same route
CHECK: load i64, ptr %arg.slot
CHECK: call i32 @_M5Store_readingZZMRBMLC5StoreZMQMLPi(ptr %s, i64
// and a constructor's, which is where this was first seen to crash
CHECK: load i64, ptr %arg.slot
CHECK: call void @_RowZZMQMLPi(ptr noalias sret(%Row)
CHECK: i64
